  "content": "<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Parma <a href=\"/blog/what-is-court\" class=\"internal-link\" title=\"court\">court</a>\" <a href=\"/blog/what-is-municipal-court\" class=\"internal-link\" title=\"Municipal Court\">Municipal Court</a></h1>\n\n<p><strong>Address:</strong> 5555 Powers Blvd, Parma, OH 44129</p>\n<p><strong>Phone:</strong> (440) 887-7400</p>\n\n<p>The Parma Municipal Court was developed in 1952 of Ohio revised code. The area of the Court of Parma municipal is 71.9sq. Miles. Perma municipal Court has 30,000 filling traffic and 177,964 citizens, criminals, and parking. It has located in Cuyahoga County, Ohio. The authority of this Court is Broadview Heights, County Agencies, Brooklyn Heights, and approximately ten other states, Brooklyn, Linndale, Seven Hills, Parma, and Parma Heights.</p>\n\n<p>If you want to release a Court ticket, you need to know that the Parma municipal holds a session every Friday at 10:30 except on holidays. If you did not attend, you must pay a heavy fine. The most important thing is that if you do not fulfil the fine, then the chances of that acceptable increase daily. Parma Municipal Court number is (440)887-7400, and the address is 5555 Powers Blvd, Parma, OH 44129.</p>\n\n<style>.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63\"]{font-style:normal;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63 mark.kt-highlight, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63\"] mark.kt-highlight{font-style:normal;color:#f76a0c;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone;box-decoration-break:clone;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63 img.kb-inline-image, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63\"] img.kb-inline-image{width:150px;vertical-align:baseline;}</style>\n<h2 class=\"kt-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading\" data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_91f3f8-63\"><strong>How To Do Parma Municipal Court Case Lookup?</strong></h2>\n\n<p>Numerous people are confused about how to do Parma Court case lookup and are applying different methods. But we will try to determine some simple ways to do case lookup. If you are trying to do case lookup, then case search and record research is best. You can quickly get it.</p>\n\n<p>see also The <a href=\"/blog/what-is-circuit-court\" class=\"internal-link\" title=\"Circuit Court\">Circuit Court</a> Of Appeals\"><a href=\"/blog/second-circuit-court-of-appeals\" class=\"internal-link\" title=\"Second Circuit Court Of Appeals\">Second Circuit Court Of Appeals</a></p>\n\n<style>.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81\"]{font-style:normal;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81 mark.kt-highlight, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81\"] mark.kt-highlight{font-style:normal;color:#f76a0c;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone;box-decoration-break:clone;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81 img.kb-inline-image, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81\"] img.kb-inline-image{width:150px;vertical-align:baseline;}</style>\n<h2 class=\"kt-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading\" data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_a4c0e2-81\">Do Parma courts deal in Small Claims?</h2>\n\n<p>Yes, per legislation and following laws, you can be an applicant to find a Suit for the Court. For further details, you can contact at small Claim Department of Court. </p>\n\n<p>Dail : (440) 887-7400 – Ext. 3</p>\n\n<p>Fax: (440) 887-7477</p>\n\n<style>.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0\"]{font-style:normal;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0 mark.kt-highlight, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0\"] mark.kt-highlight{font-style:normal;color:#f76a0c;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone;box-decoration-break:clone;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0 img.kb-inline-image, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0\"] img.kb-inline-image{width:150px;vertical-align:baseline;}</style>\n<h2 class=\"kt-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading\" data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_057ab2-d0\">Is Parma Court dealing with Civil Suit?</h2>\n\n<p>Yes, Parma Court is available for Civil kinds of suits; for that, You have to Follow the General Procedure; you can do it in Person or By sending secure Mail or by Fax. For further details, you can contact at the following information for more details.</p>\n\n<p>Phone: (440) 887-7400 – Option 3</p>\n\n<p>Fax: (440) 887-7477</p>\n\n<style>.kb-image3429_5fa97b-27.kb-image-is-ratio-size, .kb-image3429_5fa97b-27 .kb-image-is-ratio-size{max-width:1024px;width:100%;}.wp-block-kadence-column > .kt-inside-inner-col > .kb-image3429_5fa97b-27.kb-image-is-ratio-size, .wp-block-kadence-column > .kt-inside-inner-col > .kb-image3429_5fa97b-27 .kb-image-is-ratio-size{align-self:unset;}.kb-image3429_5fa97b-27 figure{max-width:1024px;}.kb-image3429_5fa97b-27 .image-is-svg, .kb-image3429_5fa97b-27 .image-is-svg img{width:100%;}.kb-image3429_5fa97b-27 .kb-image-has-overlay:after{opacity:0.3;border-top-left-radius:50px;border-top-right-radius:50px;border-bottom-right-radius:50px;border-bottom-left-radius:50px;}.kb-image3429_5fa97b-27 img.kb-img, .kb-image3429_5fa97b-27 .kb-img img{border-top-left-radius:50px;border-top-right-radius:50px;border-bottom-right-radius:50px;border-bottom-left-radius:50px;}</style>\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-image kb-image3429_5fa97b-27\"><figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"https://thecourtdirect.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/ezgif-1024x683.webp\" alt=\"Order\" class=\"kb-img wp-image-1921\" title=\"\" srcset=\"https://thecourtdirect.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/ezgif-1024x683.webp 1024w, https://thecourtdirect.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/ezgif-300x200.webp 300w, https://thecourtdirect.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/ezgif-768x512.webp 768w, https://thecourtdirect.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/ezgif-1536x1024.webp 1536w, https://thecourtdirect.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/09/ezgif-2048x1365.webp 2048w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></figure></div>\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How To File a Case?</strong></h2>\n\n<style>.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32\"]{font-style:normal;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32 mark.kt-highlight, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32\"] mark.kt-highlight{font-style:normal;color:#f76a0c;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone;box-decoration-break:clone;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32 img.kb-inline-image, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32\"] img.kb-inline-image{width:150px;vertical-align:baseline;}</style>\n<p class=\"kt-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading\" data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_e62ce7-32\"> There is a standard procedure to carry on The Court proceeding, </p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>U.S. Mail Filing</strong></h3>\n\n<style>.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70\"]{font-style:normal;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70 mark.kt-highlight, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70\"] mark.kt-highlight{font-style:normal;color:#f76a0c;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone;box-decoration-break:clone;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70 img.kb-inline-image, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70\"] img.kb-inline-image{width:150px;vertical-align:baseline;}</style>\n<p class=\"kt-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading\" data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_e034e7-70\">you can File via Mail System, and You can send the details to the Court </p>\n\n<p>You must make up the Documentation of all the processes using the Protected Mail. You can send that to the Clerk of the Court. Once the Court receives it, they shall Soumon both of the parties.</p>\n\n<p>Martin E. Vittardi, Clerk of Court</p>\n\n<p>Parma Municipal Court</p>\n\n<p>5555 Powers Boulevard Parma, Ohio 44129-5462</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>In Person Filing</strong></h3>\n\n<style>.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55\"]{font-style:normal;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55 mark.kt-highlight, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55\"] mark.kt-highlight{font-style:normal;color:#f76a0c;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone;box-decoration-break:clone;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55 img.kb-inline-image, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55\"] img.kb-inline-image{width:150px;vertical-align:baseline;}</style>\n<p class=\"kt-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading\" data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_4a80cf-55\">Another Way is Person Filing in the Court. You can connect with Court timings till 4:30 for the Clerk under the Ohio Law. For criminal, Civil and Traffic violation</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Facsimile Filing</strong></h3>\n\n<p>In the modern era, the fax method is a little antiquated, but you can still fax any paper document if you want to. What matters is that You must adhere to Local Court Rule 6. If you file documents electronically, you don't need to send them back to the court unless a case is closed by a judgement entry. While only (440) 887-7490 or (440) 887-7481 is used as a fax number. Call (440) 887-7490 for criminal matters, or (440) 887-7477 for civil cases. Your facsimile machine's created Fax Transmittal Sheet serves as your documentation that the document was filed.</p>\n\n<style>.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98\"]{font-style:normal;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98 mark.kt-highlight, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98\"] mark.kt-highlight{font-style:normal;color:#f76a0c;-webkit-box-decoration-break:clone;box-decoration-break:clone;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;}.wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98 img.kb-inline-image, .wp-block-kadence-advancedheading.kt-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98[data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98\"] img.kb-inline-image{width:150px;vertical-align:baseline;}</style>\n<h2 class=\"kt-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading\" data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading3429_a080d6-98\">Final Verdict</h2>\n\n<p>In this article, we have discussed Parma Municipal Court and detail like email address, phone number, location, what is minimum qualification before becoming a clerk in Court. If you are finding local court cases, they should use public access to electric Records. If you find the result of the Court cases, then you can contact the person who asked you to come to Court. Court dockets are one the best way to hear instances online. If you want to listen to cases online, then this is best for you. Cases files are available on the internet. </p>\n\n<p>see also The <a href=\"/blog/first-circuit-court-of-appeals\" class=\"internal-link\" title=\"First Circuit Court Of Appeals\">First Circuit Court Of Appeals</a></p>\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>FAQ:</strong></h3>\n\n<style>.kb-row-layout-id3429_5b732b-63 > .kt-row-column-wrap{align-content:start;}:where(.kb-row-layout-id3429_5b732b-63 > .kt-row-column-wrap) > .wp-block-kadence-column{justify-content:start;}.kb-row-layout-id3429_5b732b-63 > .kt-row-column-wrap{column-gap:var(--global-kb-gap-md, 2rem);row-gap:var(--global-kb-gap-md, 2rem);padding-top:0px;padding-bottom:0px;grid-template-columns:repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));}.kb-row-layout-id3429_5b732b-63 > .kt-row-layout-overlay{opacity:0.30;}@media all and (max-width: 1024px){.kb-row-layout-id3429_5b732b-63 > .kt-row-column-wrap{grid-template-columns:repeat(2, 